 "about": [
  "REQ-DEV-041 regex dialect cases (asancart documents api/device-api.md: T2.15, T3.55, T2.16, T3.56, T2.17, T2.18), the shared case set every engine runs. Not SMS data.",
  "allowed: inside the dialect; each text is matched after REQ-DEV-050's always-on steps, as a full match: the text matches ^(?:P)$ (REQ-DEV-041); groups lists named groups for some texts (null: did not take part).",
  "flag i folds ASCII letters only (T2.18): every engine rewrites the pattern (k to [kK], [a-f] to [a-fA-F]) and compiles it without its own case-insensitive option.",
  "refused: outside the dialect; tokens are the code dialect details, one per distinct token, in order of first occurrence.",
  "regex: inside the dialect, but no engine compiles it (code regex).",
  "Run on the JVM by :core:test, on Android's ICU by the app's instrumented tests, and against JavaScript RegExp (the admin engine's library) by scripts/check-dialect-cases.mjs."
 ],
